 angle, straight down included, so deep water hides the bottom and shows the water's own colour (before, deep water took the sand-coloured default Murk Colour and let a quarter of the bottom through); Water Body Murk Tint (0.3); shallows (2 m or less) unchanged. Also ([seasons], 1.2.406 folded in): new [Debugging] AsyncLog (default off, read at game start): EBM's log lines are written by a background thread; errors still at once. Ships ebm_indirect + ebm_indirect_linux. // 1.2.405 ([visual] 11-16): a small CPU trim, no setting and no look change: the hook on the game's physics push-up (called many times a second for rocks and objects) finds EBM's covered object by a lookup instead of a component search. // 1.2.404 ([visual] 11-15): fixes, no setting and no look change: with the indirect renderer stood down (or empty) the reflection-probe and other cameras no longer run an empty cull that logged "Thread group size must be above zero" about once a second; and the indirect renderer's end-of-frame step returns at once while it is stood down. // 1.2.403 ([visual] 11-15): [Optimize] WaterVanillaDistanceDetail is now ON by default: EBM's water gives distant water the game's own amount of wave detail and shares the game's screen copy (Deep North: 0.14 ms faster, no slower than the game's water; Fire passed the look with it on). The water shader itself stays off by default. A cfg that already holds the key keeps its value. // 1.2.402 ([visual] 11-15): new [Optimize] InstancedPiecesDrawLate (live, default off): baked pieces of EBM's instanced path draw after the terrain and rocks, so pieces hidden behind them are not shaded (at the Deep North pose they shaded 19 times the pixels the game's own pieces did). Defaults: [Optimize] IndirectSelfGate is now ON (marks 12000 / 15500): the indirect renderer stands down by itself where little is loaded, where it measured slower (Deep North 3.418 -> 3.261 ms, circN 4.364 -> 3.690) and stays on where it wins (bf1 4.556 against 6.617). [Water - Surface & Reflection] Game Ripples is now ON (Fire: "the ripples look good and should default on"; the water shader itself stays off by default). [Optimize] DestroyDistantBandSweep is now ON ([seasons]): after you travel away, the old area's objects are removed on the next pass instead of up to a minute later (travel leg: old zones gone 9-11 s after arrival, worst frame 51 ms against 121 ms off). A cfg that already holds these keys keeps its values. // 1.2.401 ([visual] 11-15): new [Optimize] IndirectSelfGate (live, default off): the indirect renderer stands down by itself where little is loaded (it cost 0.1 ms more than it saved at Deep North) and comes back where much is, a few groups and objects a frame, no hitch; IndirectSelfGateDownAt / UpAt are its two marks, IndirectSelfGateForce is for testing. Fixes: with no instance live the shadow caster command buffers no longer stay on the sun and lights replaying old draws; the grass compute passes stop when no grass patch is live; the "[Fill] ... settled" line is Info once, then Debug. Also ([seasons]): objects queued for removal after you travel away can no longer be dropped from the queue by an old stamp (a just-left base stayed loaded up to a minute longer); new [Optimize] DestroyDistantBandSweep (live, default OFF until its travel leg): objects left in the far part of the loaded area are removed on the next pass, as the game does. // 1.2.400 ([visual] 11-15): new [Water - Surface & Reflection] Game Ripples (live, default off): over deeper water the small ripples on EBM's water are built the way the game's own water builds them (its ripple texture three layers deep at the game's scale, lined up with the wind), so near water carries the same pattern as the far water (Fire: the near water's waves read flat and broke at the far edge; EBM's two layers were 2 to 3.7 times larger than the game's). Water 2 m deep or less keeps EBM's ripples. Off = unchanged. Ships ebm_indirect + ebm_indirect_linux. // 1.2.399 ([visual] 11-15): new [Water - Colour & Depth] Depth Colour Shift (live, default OFF until Fire's look check): the haze in the water loses red first, then green, then blue with the length of the view through it (clear shallows -> green-teal -> blue, as real water; rates from Absorption Colour Loss), and keeps the hue of Murk Colour in any sunlight (Fire: the deeper water read brown in warm sun). The amount of haze is not raised, and water 2 m deep or less is not changed at all (Fire: the shallows are right). Also new [Water - Surface & Reflection] Sky Reflection Boost (live, default 0 = off): deep water at low angles shows more of the sky reflection it already samples. Ships ebm_indirect + ebm_indirect_linux. // 1.2.398 ([visual] 11-15): with [Water - Colour & Depth] Game Water Colours on, the water's colour and opacity build with the length of your view through the water at EVERY depth, as the game's own water does (Fire: deep water stayed see-through to the bed unless there was a wave; the depth cover only acted where the water was under 8-16 m deep). "Shallow Water Colour Distance" is then the distance over which the bed fades out, everywhere. Key off = unchanged. Ships ebm_indirect + ebm_indirect_linux. // 1.2.397 ([visual] 11-15): new [Water - Colour & Depth] Game Water Colours (live, default OFF until Fire's look check): EBM's water mixes its colours as the game's own water does (dark deep / shallow colours, the bright top colour only on wave crests, the sea bed in its own colour through the water); Fire: the near water read green / tan beside the game's blue far water in the same frame. Off = 1.2.396's colours. Also new, same section: Water Lit By Waves (live, default OFF until his look check): the water's colour is lit at each pixel's wave normal, as the game's water is, instead of one light value for the whole surface. Ships ebm_indirect + ebm_indirect_linux. // 1.2.396 ([visual] 11-15): new [Optimize] WaterVanillaDistanceDetail (live, default OFF until Fire's hand test): EBM's water subdivides its surface by the game's own distance rule (full detail within 10 m, none past about 40 m, blended) and shares the game's screen copy (Deep North capture: 64 hidden water tile draws 1.13 ms against the game's 0.44 ms for the same tiles; one full-screen copy less). Off = 1.2.395's water, untouched (the shader carries a second SubShader for the key). Ships ebm_indirect + ebm_indirect_linux. // 1.2.395 ([visual] 11-15): an untouched mine rock (MineRock with a base model) is drawn as vanilla shows it, the base model alone; the indirect coverage had also drawn its ~20 breakable area meshes, which vanilla keeps switched off until the rock is hit (Plains: 680 extra instances on 34 rocks, frame 5.31 -> 4.93 ms without them in one launch). Keyless. // 1.2.394 ([visual] 11-15): the indirect presize record counts the peak slots in use with IndirectSlotTrim off too (a key turned on mid-session saved the count after a compaction, and the next load grew its buffers once); the record never drops below half of what it held at load (one session away from the dense place, or one killed early in a load, no longer collapses it; [seasons] / [lead]); one Debug line "[Indirect] instance buffers re-made: ..." at each growth or trim re-make of the instance buffers. No key, no default change. // 1.2.393 ([visual] 11-15): [Optimize] IndirectSlotCompact default false -> true ([lead]: its gate leg at ocean, clean A/B: frame 4.616 -> 4.443 ms, nothing dropped, worst frame of the pass 0.85 ms; Plains unchanged); [Optimize] IndirectSlotTrim default false -> true ([lead]: speed 0, frees memory: 18 MB of slot arrays in its A/B leg at ocean, 54 MB from a 524288-slot capacity; frame 4.399 -> 4.407 ms); the presize uses the slot capacity of an old record again (with IndirectSlotTrim on it was discarded, so the first load of a world grew its buffers by doubling; [seasons] / [lead]); the WaterTessCut description now reads as a key that is off by default ([seasons]). No saved value is rewritten. // 1.2.392: [Optimize] WaterTessCut default true -> false ([lead]: its legs showed no gain; never shipped). 1.2.392 COMPACT ([visual] 11-15, [lead]; Plains census: "Instances 100646 live in 227922 slots" before an IndirectRenderer off -> on, "99970 live in 99970 slots" after, the cycle worth 0.31 ms at Plains and 0.26 ms at ocean): [Optimize] IndirectSlotCompact (live, default off until its leg): once a load settles, live instances move down into the free slots so s_high = the live count; owners are patched (group slot lists; IndirectBatches handles are now ids into a table); orphan instances are counted and named, nothing is removed. The compaction is sliced (0.5 ms a frame) and prints what it took. Upload now also sends a freed top slot (its zero batch id). Also ([seasons]): the [Cache] 30 s line no longer counts reads of kept old-settings files as zones baked fresh; MeshBaker forgets a zone's piece classes at its unload (destroyed pieces stayed as dead keys) and its dead-key sweep is time-sliced; EbmMeshCheck trims its scratch lists. // 1.2.391 WATER ([visual] 11-15, [lead]; Fire: never worse than vanilla; Deep North toggle run: EBM/Water cost 0.135 ms a frame with no water on screen): [Optimize] WaterTessCut (live, ON) + WaterTessFarStart / WaterTessFarEnd: EBM/Water no longer tessellates patches outside the view and lowers the factor on far zone tiles; needs the 1.2.391 ebm_indirect bundles. // 1.2.390 ([seasons] 11-15, found by [visual] in the 1.2.389 mountain leg: alloc 9021 KB/s vs 1503): a saved zone file that is read and not usable ([Cache] KeepOtherSettings: baked under another settings fingerprint) is remembered, so the near pump of [Cache] PreloadSlim / PreloadNearOnly no longer reads it again every 2 s and it no longer counts as a saved bake; the near worker keeps its read buffer.   // 1.2.389 SLOT TRIM ([visual] for [seasons]' tree, [lead]: "presize to the live need + headroom, and shrink when live < 1/4 of capacity for a while"; rig: 524288 slots of capacity for 9-15 k in use = 75.5 MB): [Optimize] IndirectSlotTrim (live, default off until its leg): the presize record keeps the session's peak slots in use instead of the capacity, and the slot arrays + instance buffers shrink after 60 s under a quarter used. // 1.2.389 MEMORY ([seasons] 11-15, [lead]; Fire: part of the town stays in memory): [Cache] PreloadSlim (live, default off until the census leg): a built zone's saved copy leaves managed memory once its file holds the same bake, unbuilt zones are held near the player only, a zone reached sooner is read from its file on demand (no rebuild after a teleport). [Heap] census lines at Info on the first line / an 8 MB change / ebm_heap. [Cache] ZdoCombineIdleRelease (live, default off): the ZDO bake's copies of the prefab meshes (48 B a vertex, held until world close) are freed after 60 s without use and re-read on demand. Key off = 1.2.388 behaviour.   // 1.2.388 MIST ([visual] 11-14, [lead]; Fire: "It's the mist itself that causes the problems for performance"): [Optimize] MistShader (live, ON): the two Lux mist materials draw with EBM/MistLux (no tessellation; ported from our FTS FiresMistLux), [Optimize] MistParticleCount / MistOpacity (live, 1 = vanilla) tune the ParticleMist emitter, EbmApi.HandlesShader claims "Lux Lit Particles/ Tess Bumped". // 1.2.388 ([visual] 11-14, [lead]; Fire: the Mistlands gap vs the rival; 11-13 gcircle3 O log "record cascades 0.023" ms a frame while "8815 of 9228 frame(s) reused the last cell verdict"): [Optimize] IndirectCascadeScanReuse (live, default off until its leg): the per-frame shadow-cascade scan is skipped while nothing it reads changed; [Optimize] IndirectCullBindCache ([seasons]' draft; live, default off): the cull kernel's buffer binds only when one changed; the [Indirect] 30-s line gains the caster material changes per cascade and the scans skipped. // 1.2.387 ([seasons] 11-14, [lead]): [Cache] ZdoFirstBake default false -> true (a saved value is NOT changed: no migration); its description and its first-use Info line no longer say "prototype" / "no cache file is written" (false since 1.2.374).   // 1.2.386 ([seasons] 11-14, [lead]): one Info line "[Cache] ZdoFirstBake since the zones were last reset (...)" with zones built from ZDOs / files written / swaps done, at the OFF flip and at the zone reset (world close, plugin disable); silent when the path built nothing.   // 1.2.385 ([visual] 11-14, [lead]; Fire: "All of those extra shader checks for ebm's heightmap shouldn't even run outside of vedr winter" / "get it fixed"): EBM/Heightmap's exact work skips are always on (the six [Optimize] TerrainCheap* keys are no longer read; a saved false no longer makes every ground pixel pay the snow-mud taps), two more exact skips in the shader (mud taps only where a trail makes mud; tessellation-stage paint taps only where the vertex has snow or ash weight); verify switch [Debugging] TerrainExactSkipsOff; new ebm_indirect bundle. // 1.2.384 ([seasons] 11-14, [lead]): ebm_coldcache ends when the world closes (ZNetScene.Shutdown), so a logout / login to the same world in the same launch is back on the real cache folder; one Info line when it was on. [visual]: one Info line per live flip of IndirectFarCardShadows / IndirectMergedCasters with the cascade caster draws before -> after.   // 1.2.383 ([visual] 11-14, [lead]; town run O_20261114_163205: two live keys flipped with "0" and nothing told an empty walk from a scene without targets): every live-flip Info line reports walked / seen / acted (ZSyncStaticSkip, ParticleIdlePause, RemoteItemZSyncSkip, GpuFires, IndirectCoverage on and off); log text only, no behaviour change. // 1.2.382 ([seasons] 11-14, [lead]; Fire: off / on tests inside one run): console command ebm_coldcache on | off | status: this session's saved zones move to an empty test folder (<world>_client_coldtest; the real folder untouched and not read), so TD can run cold first-visit arms in one launch; no key, never saved.   // 1.2.381 ([visual] 11-14, [lead], hot-swap audit 4c: the town / movement keys that are toggled live): ZSyncStaticSkipEnabled (+ Fixtures) re-enables what it disabled on OFF and takes the loaded pieces on ON; [Batching] ParticleIdlePause, RemoteItemZSyncSkipEnabled and GpuFires take the loaded objects on ON; IndirectCoverage flipped alone hands every covered object back (its instances leave the tables) or attaches the loaded ones. // 1.2.380 ([seasons] + [visual] 11-14, [lead], Fire: off/on tests toggle keys live in one run; Tools/HOTSWAP_EBM_KEYS_20261114.md): live-flip fixes. [Cache] ZdoFirstBake off drops its work in progress ([seasons]); IdleGates sets its tracked particle systems to the key's side on a flip; the depth pyramid and vegetation prepass camera buffers leave the camera when their keys or IndirectRenderer go off; IndirectFarCardShadows / IndirectCasterMinScreen re-record the cascades once on a change; DestroyTimeSliceEnabled off clears its queue. // 1.2.379 ([seasons] + [visual] 11-14, [lead]: 1.2.378 first-visit leg 1535_2P, the hilltop spire still missing although every zone was filed and swapped): the this-visit swap brings the file's instance GROUPS too (their live pieces silenced through the same budgeted queue), runs for a file without batches and, groups only, after a re-save; one file ask per zone while its piece count is the one the file was built from (42 saves for 28 zones). // 1.2.378 ([visual] + [seasons] 11-14, [lead] / Fire "so the cache is correct"): the ZDO background FILE job takes the bake-safe non-skippable invulnerable pieces exactly as the live bake does (groups at the minimum, the combine otherwise), so a ZDO-built file equals a live-built one (1.2.377 verifier: MISSING hard 18 = feeders of a batch that only reached MinPiecesPerBatch with those pieces; MISSING allowed 1763); the file job waits on the zone's PIECE count standing still, not on sector arrivals. Small: vegetation prepass 30-s line first Info then Debug; [Batching] IdleGatesCullingMode (1.2.366 test key) removed, PauseAndCatchup kept; camera draw sort mode Info on change; Integrity scale note needs an implausible box. // 1.2.377 ([visual] + [seasons] 11-14, [lead]: the 1.2.375 full-bake chain's bugs): the ZDO path's low-count rules are MeshBaker's own (OnlyInstancingCanDrawFromZdo / LowCountDamageableOnlyFromZdo: a below-minimum damageable key of a combiner-refused prefab no longer gets a group the live bake does not make: verifier EXTRA darkwood roofs / vines / ashwood floors), the combiner verdict falls back to the prefab asset; [seasons]: verifier timing, save rule reach, second visit. // 1.2.376 ([seasons] 11-14, [lead], Fire's light scenes): [Optimize] IndirectCameraDrawSort (0 / 1 / 2, default 0): the baked batches' camera draws in state order, mode 2 with one shared bounds for the opaque ones (SetPass 651 for 668 draws at Mistlands spot3 vs the rival's 491 for 827). Transparent batches and shadow draws unchanged.   // 1.2.375 ([visual] + [seasons] 11-14, [lead]): the ZDO full bake's verifier gets a TRUE batch parity for town zones: the pieces the live bake merged but the ZDO file leaves live are taken off the live side (ZdoCombine.PartCounts) before the batches are compared; a batch on one side only is reported apart. Verifier only ([Optimize] ZdoBakeVerify); no behaviour change. // 1.2.374 ([visual] + [seasons] 11-14, Fire via [lead]: "use the one method to load the zone faster and then while we're in the area it properly bakes in the background so the cache is correct"): with [Cache] ZdoFirstBake on, a ZDO-baked zone gets its FULL bake in the background: combined batches built from prefab meshes + ZDO matrices on a worker thread (EasyBake\ZdoCombine.cs, no live pieces, no Mesh.CombineMeshes), saved as a normal full cache file once the sector is quiet. [Cache] ZdoBakeSaveGroups (1.2.373 test key, groups-only files) removed. // 1.2.373 ([seasons] 11-14, Fire "test it properly", [lead]): [Cache] ZdoBakeSaveGroups (default off): a ZDO-baked zone saves its groups-only cache file once its sector is quiet, never over an existing file. Also [Cache] ZdoFirstBakeBudgetMs default 2 -> 0 (the cold budget ABBA: slicing lost on every column). Saved values untouched.   // 1.2.372 ([visual] 11-14, [lead] approved): [Optimize] CascadeAppendOnGain, default off: a cascade that GAINS a caster batch gets the new rows appended to its shadow command buffer instead of a clear + full re-record of all four (cold-entry capture O_20261114_104123: "EBM casters: re-record" 1.5 ms in 56 of 82 worst-window frames); full re-record kept for layout / light / epoch / moved batch, stale > 25 %, appended > 25 %; Debug reasons + appends on the [Indirect] line, marker "EBM casters: append". // 1.2.371 ([seasons] 11-14, [lead]): [Cache] ZdoFirstBake scans sliced under [Cache] ZdoFirstBakeBudgetMs (default 2): "attach early, keep filling" (a creation ask attaches the zone with what is classified, the scan keeps filling its groups; created-before-its-slice pieces draw themselves; uid checks); Debug first-sight split. Key still default off.   // 1.2.370 ([seasons] 11-14, [lead] approved): [Cache] ZdoFirstBake levers (1) nothing to instance = wait for the sector's ZDOs, not a decline; (2) CreateZone asks first (the race); per-zone Debug names the path. Key still default off.   // 1.2.369 ([seasons] 11-14, [lead] approved, [visual] cache side): [Cache] ZdoFirstBake PROTOTYPE, default off (EasyBake\ZoneTrackerZdoBake.cs). 1.2.368 ([seasons] 11-14, [lead]/[visual]): [Cache] SaveSliced default true -> false (cold pair 2 not a win: more >50 ms hitches and worse worst frames with it ON; 5-s and 1 % lows tie). Saved values untouched. Nothing else changes.   // 1.2.367 ([seasons] + [visual] 11-14, [lead]: markers + Debug text only, no behaviour change): "EBM indirect: <phase>" on the EndFrame phases (EbmIndirectPhases names) and "EBM draw: ..." on ZoneTracker.DrawInstances' DwSeg segments (tail row "EBM LateUpdate: DrawInstances" 1.24 vs 0.86 ms, all self); "EBM Update: <tick>" on every Plugin.Update tick (GC row "Plugin.Update() > GC.Alloc" 2.17 KB/frame); [visual]'s "EBM casters: re-record" scope + per-cascade recorded draw counts on the [Indirect] Debug line.   // 1.2.366 ([seasons] 11-14, [lead]/[visual], row T6 load-screen ParticleSystem.Update): TEST build (staged B arm, not live) with [Batching] IdleGatesCullingMode = PauseAndCatchup (default = 1.2.365) | Pause | Off for the looping particle systems IdleGates handles on placed pieces. (2) [Optimize] BakeGateSliced default true -> false: no win warm or cold ([visual]'s cold pair 1: OFF 11.52 ms / 30 hitches / 127.5 worst vs ON 11.74 / 31 / 128.6; 26-28 zones baked per leg); saved values untouched.   // 1.2.365 ([seasons] 11-14, FIRE ORDER via [lead]): BlackFrameWatch (1.2.359, [visual]) commented out behind #if EBM_BLACKFRAME (its file body + the Bind and Tick calls here): not bound, not installed, not run; source kept to re-enable for debugging; its cfg keys stay orphaned (no rewrite). Nothing else changes.   // 1.2.364 ([seasons] 11-14): (1) SyncSnowKeyword asks the SHADER for a Float/Range _AddSnow on source AND clone (EbmIndirectAssets.ShaderHasAddSnow) instead of Material.HasProperty, which is true for a saved value the shader lacks: [generator]'s grep, 132 Unity warnings "Material '<x>_lowlod' with Shader 'Custom/Piece' doesn't have a float or range property '_AddSnow'"; rocks unchanged. (2) BakeSettle's once-per-zone "bake held until N s" line Info -> Debug (52 lines in a 4 min leg; the 1.2.363 diagnostic leg proved each disk log line a synchronous flush, up to 433 ms). (3) [lead] Info-vs-Debug audit: EasyBakeLog.InfoFirst(key, msg) = first per session at Info, the rest at Debug, for the lines that repeat while playing: [Stream] queue drained, [SelfCost] LateUpdate 30 s, [Cache] last 30 s, [Transition] last 30 s, [Transition] support damage held, [Indirect] main-thread phases 30 s, [Indirect] vegetation prepass, [Arrival] waiting (long waits), [ZoneLoad] kept.   // 1.2.363 ([seasons] 11-14, [visual] read of the 1.2.362 circle O_20261114_005404): markers + reasons only, to name the open rows before slicing: SaveZone split + an Info line when a save is NOT sliced and why ("save zone" 377.9 ms SELF again); the checks phase split per call + per zone built from cache ("EBM checks" 611.6 ms); the gate's variation walk apart from BakeSettle + an Info naming any one piece whose check takes 20 ms+ ("gates" 350.5 ms in one frame); CacheSummary build vs log write (~50 ms every 30 s).   // 1.2.362 ([seasons] 11-14, from [visual]'s read of the 1.2.361 town circle O_20261114_003628): BakeGateSliced budget is now ONE per frame shared by all due zones (1.2.361 gave 1 ms per zone call: "EBM bake:settle + variation gates" 263 ms over 5 stall frames); markers only for the 108 ms "pump: sliced cache saves" step (batch / finish / E25 re-read) and the 75-115 ms pacer tail (signals / fill note / reconcile); [lead]: the zone walk's steps ("EBM walk:*", for "EBM walking zones" 260 ms once) and every LateUpdate call ("EBM LateUpdate: *", for its unattributed 117 ms once). Markers are using (m.Auto()) only.   // 1.2.361 ([seasons] 11-13, Fire: "make the reads, get the fixes in"): [Cache] SaveSliced (default on, + SaveSliceBudgetMs 2): the bake pass's cache save, the worst EBM stall step on the 1.2.360 marker capture ("frame 250: 358.3 ms; top self: EBM bake:save zone 342.4 ms"), reads its meshes one batch per step over the next frames instead of all in the bake frame (MeshCacheStore.TrySaveSliced / PumpSlicedSaves); Restore finishes a pending save (a dirty rebake drops it), Delete drops it, E25 release waits for it. Off = as 1.2.360. (2) [Optimize] BakeGateSliced (default on): the pre-bake material-variation check ("EBM bake:settle + variation gates" 77.5 / 67.7 ms) remembers a clear zone and walks at most ~1 ms of pieces a frame. (3) pacer pass ("EBM patch:pacer CreateObjects pass" 259.6 ms