he new default reaches cfgs.  // 1.2.201 ([ghost] EasyBakeIntactRockLod.cs, DESIGN_OcclusionLOD Â§5, lead approved 11-08; frozen by [visual]): A/B key [Optimize] BakeIntactRocks (default off = vanilla rocks): after vanilla MineRock5.UpdateMesh, an intact rock draws one SHARED copy of vanilla's own combined mesh per prefab (its private copy freed) and, with Core 0.2.1212+'s FiresCore.Far.MeshSimplify (by name), a shared simplified LOD1 below IntactRockLod1ScreenHeight (0.8) at IntactRockLod1Detail (48) cells; the first damage gives the rock vanilla's mesh and LODGroup back; colliders untouched; key off restores all. ebm_rocks prints the "[Rocks] bake" line.  // 1.2.200 (DESIGN_OcclusionLOD 2b, lead approved 11-08, TOWN50): A/B key [Optimize] InstancedInstanceCull (default off = as 1.2.199): one worker thread (EasyBakeInstanceCull.cs) tests every instance bounds sphere against the main camera frustum (fov +15 %, pushed out by camera travel) with a conservative sun sweep (kept when d(c) + 1.5 x shadowDistance x max(0, n.sunDir) >= -r on every plane, so no caster whose shadow can reach the view is dropped); the group keeps ONE compacted matrix list (+ part lists + size-classed snow arrays) and rebuilds it only when the visible set changes; a turn over 10 deg or a 20 m jump since the job draws everything that frame; other cameras keep the full lists. Debug [Draw]: part instances submitted of held, compacted rebuilds, worker ms.  // 1.2.199 (TOWN50, lead / [classes-ui] approved 11-08 after cells lost on calls): [Optimize] InstancedShadowProxies and InstancedCellLod no longer need cell runs: every draw goes through DrawRun (group bounds without cells). A shadow proxy (main draw casts nothing + one ShadowsOnly draw one LOD below what is drawn; the zone far tier counts as LOD1) is made ONLY for parts whose prefab has that lower LOD, so parts without one cost no extra call. Both keys default off = as 1.2.198. [Draw]: proxy shadow tris + shadow-only calls a frame.  // 1.2.198 ([saddles] FAP 1.1.407 / [generator] audit, 11-08): add-only event FiresEasyBakeMeshes.EbmBakedPieces.PieceLeftBake(GameObject), raised on the main thread from EasyBakeSuppressedVisuals.RestoreVisuals (the one point a live piece the bake drew gets its renderers back); Draws() now also answers false while the zone has a hand-back in flight (AwaitingRecreate), so a handed-back piece never defers. A throwing listener is removed after one Warning. Cell-mode fixes from the TOWN50 cell-16 leg (submit 4.7 -> 19.4 ms, GPU 29 -> 53 ms, GC 3 per 5 s): each snow range's instanced arrays are sized to its run (power of two 8..1023, block replaced only when the size class changes; was two 1023-float arrays per run, uploaded whole each draw); one shared cell-sort comparer (was a closure per sort); no tuple-array per re-split; the [Draw] tris split counts the zone far tier as far again (1.2.196 counted it as near: "far mesh 0k" was the proof line, not the draw).  // 1.2.197 (lead 11-08): (a) [ghost]'s read-only ebm_rocks [radius m] console report (EasyBakeRockReport.cs: every MineRock5 near the camera, intact or not, LOD now / count / transition heights, tris per LOD, shadow mode; per-prefab totals), for the DESIGN_OcclusionLOD rocks lever; no patch, no behaviour change. (b) [generator] audit: add-only FiresEasyBakeMeshes.EbmBakedPieces.Draws(GameObject piece) = the bake draws this exact piece in place of its renderers (zone baked, not held real, identity among the contributors), valid from ZNetView.Awake, so visual-only Awake hooks can return early.  // 1.2.196 (DESIGN_OcclusionLOD_20261108 2b + 2c, lead approved 11-08, TOWN50): two A/B keys on the 1.2.195 cell runs, both default off = as 1.2.195. [Optimize] InstancedCellLod: each instanced part carries its prefab's LOD chain (same rule as the old LOD1 far mesh: single renderer per level, same material + submesh, same placement) and vanilla's transition heights; each cell run draws the level vanilla's LODGroup would pick at the run's nearest point (size / (2 d tan(fov/2)) x lodBias), and nothing where vanilla culls. [Optimize] InstancedShadowProxies: the run's main draw casts no shadow and a ShadowsOnly draw one LOD lower casts it. Debug [Draw] adds instances per LOD level, LOD-culled, proxy shadow tris.  // 1.2.195 (TOWN50, [classes-ui]/lead 11-08: a baked group drew with ONE zone-sized bounds, so the camera and every sun-shadow cascade got all its instances): A/B key [Optimize] InstancedCellSizeMeters (default 0 = as before): above 0, a group orders its instances by x/z cell (inside its roofed / open snow sections, values carried along) and draws one call per cell run with that run's own bounds, so Unity culls per cell for the view and for each cascade. Same look; more calls, fewer tris. Rebuilt only on an instance or key change, buffers reused. Debug [Draw] split names the key value and instances per call next to the 1.2.194 tris split.  // 1.2.194 (Fire 0108k BlueHills city on 1.2.193 + town 50 fps target, lead 11-08): (a) a cached zone is judged against its ZDOs only once FGN settled it (never on the 60 s filling ceiling) and its ZDO count was quiet 30 s (10 s without FGN); pieces missing at both looks leave their instanced groups without a rebake (the 1.2.193 city rebaked 25 cached zones for pieces the server had not sent yet, 65k pieces created live then unloaded); only pieces merged into a combined mesh still rebake; (b) a cached zone is built at FGN ZoneFilling (before its first piece is created) so its pieces are skipped at creation; (c) the Debug [Draw] split adds tris submitted a frame (near / far mesh, shadow-casting). Proof: "[StandIn] ... gone piece(s) dropped ... rebake(s) ... cached zone(s) built at FGN ZoneFilling", "[Bake] ... instanced dropped without rebake", "[Draw] ... tris submitted".  // 1.2.193 (Fire's BlueHills arrival on 1.2.192, [visual] proof: "missing 25,423: 806 skipped, 407 would be skipped, 24,179 still to create"; city zones rebaked on "(-19,12) 5,240 contributor(s), 5,110 ZDO(s) held, 595 missing", the zone not yet all delivered, so its cache was thrown away and every piece became a live object; lead GO): (b) a cache check that finds contributors missing no longer rebakes at once: it looks again at the next settle or 30 s later and rebakes only if the SAME contributors are still missing. (a)/(c) FGN 1.6.54's zone signal (FiresGhettoNetworkMod.FgnStreaming, by reflection, used only while its live flag is on): a zone FGN says is still filling is neither judged nor baked until it settles (60 s ceiling), and its identity set is rebuilt once on settle. Without FGN: EBM's own quiet windows, as 1.2.192. Debug proof: "[Bake] Zone (x,y) cache check: N missing of C -> recheck at settle / in 30 s before any rebake", "... -> rebake (same contributors still missing: K)", "... 0 missing -> cache kept (the N missing last time were delivered)", and the 10 s [StandIn] line shows the FGN signal state. No keys.   // 1.2.192 (Fire 0108i, BlueHills teleport 30 s; lead GO): an arrival (spawn / teleport) waits in vanilla IsAreaReady for every ZDO in the 3x3 to have an instance; EBM decides "skip" only when the create loop reaches a piece, so baked pieces it WILL skip counted as missing. [Optimize] ArrivalCountsBakedPieces (default ON, a fix): such a piece counts as ready once its stand-in collider exists. Debug proof "[Arrival] area at (x, z): missing N: S skipped, W would be skipped (stand-in ready), C would be skipped (no stand-in yet), K still to create -> ready / waiting" at most every 5 s.   // 1.2.191 (Fire's BlueHills city, 174k ZDOs, minutes to load; [visual] proof from his 0108h log, lead GO): (a) the stand-in pass rebuilt a zone's whole ZDO identity set (FindSectorObjects + a new HashSet, ~3,000 in a city zone) and walked it again for "real" objects on EVERY frame its queue was open ("tracking zones 0.70-0.85 ms a frame, stand-ins 0.56-0.65"); now the set lives on the zone and is rebuilt only when that sector's ZDO count changes or after 2 s, and "real" is one lookup per identity. (b) a zone built from its cache was validated against LIVE objects that EBM's own create skip never created, so every check saw "0 present" and called the whole zone removed (89 checks, 207,560 pieces); it is now validated against the zone's ZDOs, and waits while none are held or they are still arriving. Debug proof lines: "[StandIn] zone identity sets, last 10 s: N rebuilt, M reused; K cached-zone check(s) waited" and "[Bake] Zone (x,y) cache check vs ZDOs: ... -> cache kept / rebake". No keys.   // 1.2.190 (lead 11-08, 0107w/x sweep): the "[Cache] Zone (x,y): instanced prefab ... no longer resolves; discarding cache so the zone rebakes" line is Debug (was a Warning once per prefab): it is EBM healing a cache made before a mod changed that prefab (Building_VAGaziboRavensRest after the vapieces repack); the zone rebakes once and the new cache leaves the prefab out.  1.2.189 (SanEggs 11-06: Jewelcrafting's Projectile.Awake postfix threw from EBM's prewarm; Fire 11-08 "make sure ebm is safe for all mods"): the prewarm clones prefabs under an INACTIVE holder (no Awake / OnEnable / OnDestroy runs on any component, vanilla or modded) and only warms what EBM can bake or instance (building pieces, its vegetation), never projectiles, creatures, items, ships, carts or spawners; every call into another mod (Vedr, FTS, FAT, FAP, Core) is guarded: a throw gives ONE Warning naming the mod and EBM uses its own behaviour from then on; prefab lookups (ZNetScene.GetPrefab, which other mods patch) are guarded; the load coroutine survives a throw in any step; optional-mod type lookups no longer log a HarmonyX warning when the mod is absent.  1.2.188 (Fire 11-08: "indoor wet from ebm steps aside to vedr when both installed"): while VedrApi.IndoorWetActive (Vedr 0.8.183+, ApiVersion 17, live flag re-read every second) is true, the wet override leaves every renderer on Vedr/Piece to Vedr (roofed-dry and roof undersides; anything EBM had dried is handed back to the global _Wet) and baked groups drop their roofed _Wet 0 split; other shaders keep EBM's dry; ShelterRain unchanged; without Vedr as before. Debug line on each stand-down / resume.  1.2.187 (lead 11-08, 0107u zone (26,4) cache thrown away: stone_wall_1x1_triangular refused on Vedr/Piece before EBM had seen a Vedr swap): the snow-swap mapping is learned up front from the snow mods, gated on their live flag (VedrApi.PieceShaderActive for Vedr/Piece; FTS FiresPieceShaderLoader.Enabled + EnsureLoaded for Custom/FiresPiece), at the ZNetScene.Awake index and again when the gate first meets that shader; learn-on-first-sight stays the fallback; Debug line when learned up front.  1.2.186 (lead 11-08, EBM draw ~30-40 ms/s): the Debug [Draw] line adds "Split:" (main-view prep vs RenderMeshInstanced submit, calls, snow-range calls, part instances a frame; per-camera pre-cull draws by camera name, which the draw figure never counted); toggles [Optimize] InstancedFollowChecksEveryFrame and InstancedOtherCameraRedraw, both default true = as before.  1.2.185 (lead 11-08, 0107r census "8 of 5059 silenced piece(s) are in no zone's list"): the zone unload gives silenced pieces ZNetScene still holds their renderers back before it drops the list (was a bare Clear) and the reload re-adopts them; the census (now Debug on or off) heals orphans already leaked: re-adopted where the active zone's bake draws them, otherwise given back their renderers; one Info line the first time it heals.  1.2.184 (lead 11-07, Fire stone_wall_2x1 body invisible at 1635,460): Debug "[Suppress] orphan census" at most every 30 s and only after something changed: silenced pieces in no zone's SuppressedPieces list (the unload branch clears a list without restoring), first 5 with position, whether ZNetScene still holds them, their EBM zone (active / marked unloaded) and whether its bake draws them.  1.2.183 (lead 11-07, WearNTearUpdater 114 ms/s): Vedr's winter keep holds a piece kind with no vanilla snow cap real only while Vedr 0.8.170+ (VedrApi ApiVersion 16, PieceSnowCapFor) says it gets one or has not decided; kinds Vedr caps never (vines, sloped, stations) skip and bake again; answers cached per kind, undecided ones re-asked when PieceSnowCapRevision moves; older Vedr keeps the 1.2.180 behaviour.the Debug "[Skip] reasons so far" line adds "winter keep: N piece(s) of K kind(s) kept real (M with a snow cap on the prefab, V of W kind(s) only if Vedr caps them: ...)", distinct per season; the winter check builds its reason text only when it is logged.  1.2.182 (lead 11-07, snow_proof3 cache warnings): the modded-prefab gate judges a shader that a snow swap put on a material (Vedr/Piece, FTS's) as the game shader it replaced, and a prefab's verdict is taken before EBM asks for the swap, so modded pieces on Vedr/Piece bake and instance again; the cached-zone "no longer resolves" line names the prefab and why, Warn once per prefab, Debug after.  1.2.181 (Fire 11-07: piece snow moves into Vedr): baked piece snow from VedrApi (PieceSnowCover, PieceExposureAt, PieceFieldActive, ApplyPieceShader, PieceSnowRevision) when Vedr has them, FTS + Core otherwise; _VedrSnowCover written beside _FiresSnowBiome; works with Vedr alone; one Info line names the source.  1.2.180 ([seasons] 11-07, Vedr 0.8.145 snow caps on flat pieces): while Vedr builds winter snow on pieces in a biome (VedrApi.SnowBuildingBiomeMask), WearNTear pieces there are not skip-spawned, so they grow and draw snow; Vedr season change re-checks skipped pieces; Debug reason per piece kind.  1.2.179 ([seasons], Fire 11-07 pier snow): baked pieces never switch off their snow cap renderers (m_snow / m_snowWorn / m_snowBroken and children); vanilla UpdateSnowVisual owns them, so build-up shows on baked pieces. Debug "snow caps left to vanilla: N" per piece kind.  1.2.178 (Fire 11-07, longhouse in a winter storm): in shelter every falling-weather system of the current env stops, re-checked every 0.2