nge only), and a part follows a NEW material put on the prefab renderer (checked once a second); Info one-shot + Debug per follow.  // 1.2.154 ([visual], Fire 10-30 choice (a), public chest report: pieces skipped while unsupported fell when EBM was turned off): [Batching] SkipOnHost and SkipDamageablePieces default FALSE and out of the 1.2.145 defaults-on migration (a saved value stays; no forced flip); both descriptions state the support gap plainly. No logic change.  // 1.2.153 ([visual], Fire 10-30 via lead, public white-trees report: "It's not default on or be forced on"): [Batching] SkipVegetation default FALSE and no longer in the 1.2.145 defaults-on migration (a user's own saved value stays; SkipOnHost / SkipDamageablePieces unchanged).  // 1.2.152 ([visual], Fire 10-30 shot 403: one hanging brazier showed only its bowl, "low on fuel"): pieces with a Fireplace whose fire / fuel children the game toggles (m_enabledObject / High / Low) are never baked or skipped, so a bake can not freeze a fuel state; Debug "[EBM] kept live: <prefab> (toggled visuals ...)" once per prefab.  // 1.2.151 ([visual], [fgn] / lead 10-30 town walk: "not created 12174/frame (sorted every frame) ... 937.2 ms over 69 frames"): [Optimize] PartialCreateSort (default ON): the create queue is no longer sorted in full every frame; only the nearest K = max(512, 4 x budget) go first in vanilla's order (bounded heap, O(n log K)); [CreateBudget] status counts "partial" sorts.  // 1.2.150 ([visual], Fire 10-30 "if that setting makes things worse then lets get rid of it all together"): the DeferCreationWhileBaking feature is removed (EasyBake/DeferCreation.cs, its ZoneTracker hold and cfg key); a saved line in an old cfg is an orphan BepInEx ignores.  // 1.2.149 ([visual], Fire 10-30 shadow option C for the A/B): [Optimize] FarSmallNoShadows (default OFF) + NoShadowBeyondMeters (40) + NoShadowSmallerThanMeters (1): baked instanced pieces whose group is beyond the distance, or whose mesh is smaller than the size, draw without casting a sun shadow; the [Draw] Debug line counts the part draws cut.  // 1.2.148 ([visual], public report via Fire): feasts (any piece with a Feast component) are never baked.   // 1.2.147 ([visual], lead dense65 worst 41.7 ms): the snow re-split budget holds across groups: a group waits a frame when the shared budget is spent (only the frame's first re-split is guaranteed progress), budget checked every 4 instances (was a forced 16 per group: 23 groups x 14 = 313 instances = 41.7 ms); Debug summary counts deferred draws.  // 1.2.146 ([visual], lead 10-28, dense58 161.5 ms re-split): snow re-split sliced to a per-frame budget shared by all groups, cut every 16 instances inside a group (Batching / SnowResplitBudgetMs = 2, 0 = off); Debug "[SnowBake] re-split sliced: N group(s) over M frame(s), worst X ms".  //   // 1.2.145 ([visual], Fire 10-28: proven improvements never off by default): SkipOnHost, SkipDamageablePieces, SkipVegetation default ON; an existing cfg's false is moved to true ONCE (marker BepInEx\cache\FiresEasyBakeMeshes\defaults_on_1_2_145.done); Debug "[EBM] defaults-on migration".   // 1.2.144 ([visual], lead 10-28 settled snow spikes): [SnowBake] re-split timer: Debug line per frame over 20 ms (groups, instances), worst frame in the 30 s summary. No behaviour change.  //   // 1.2.143 ([visual], Fire 10-28 "Build it"): FAP/VA source lookups resolved once; the source only worked out when its Debug line is written; [Skip] sampler splits prefab scan / modded gate; EasyBakeLog.Debug writes LogDebug.   // 1.2.142 ([visual], lead 10-28): Debug-only sampler of the CreateObject skip prefix by step, one line per frame over 20 ms. 1.2.141 ([visual], 10-28 ledger: the 1.2.140 prewarm coroutine was the top stall site, 37.7 s): prewarm removed (lazy again); slow-step Debug lines kept. 1.2.140 ([visual], round 45 login stall 1139 ms, EBM CreateObject prefix 659 ms): shader index + piece prefab checks prewarmed after ZNetScene.Awake at 3 ms a frame; Debug "[EBM] prewarm: ..." and "[Skip] slow step inside CreateObject: ..." per step over 10 ms. 1.2.139 ([visual], Fire 10-27 fire shadows flashing / smelter light pool flipping): light budget never touches shadows on a LightLod light (vanilla owns them), enter 18 m / leave 22 m + 3 s hold, Debug line per flip. 1.2.138 ([visual], Fire 10-27 standing rule via lead: why/proof/summary lines are Debug only): every EasyBakeLog.Info except the loaded/active/enable lines and console-command output now writes at Debug; no behaviour change. 1.2.137 ([visual] for [ghost]'s live map ROOFS toggle, Fire 10-27): add-only FiresEasyBakeMeshes.EbmRoofs.HideRoofsFor(Camera, bool) keeps baked ROOF groups (name has "roof", not "wall_roof") out of that camera only (per-camera pre-cull draw while any camera hides them; no change otherwise) + IsRoofPrefab / IsRoofName for live pieces. 1.2.136 ([visual], Fire 10-27 YES, homestead 8 fps = x10.9 render passes from 22 point lights): [Optimize] LightBudgetEnabled (default on): only the nearest 8 build-piece lights within 20 m keep pixel lighting + shadows, the rest vertex-lit with no shadows (EasyBake/LightBudget.cs; Debug "[EBM] light budget: ..."); the 1.2.125-1.2.135 executing lines moved to Debug. 1.2.135 ([visual], overnight 10-27, lead GO): [General] PerformanceProfile = Default | LowEnd (read once at load; Default unchanged): LowEnd halves every per-frame bake / convert / stand-in / destroy / material budget and the create budget, far tier + light / SFX LOD distances x0.75; executing line. 1.2.134 ([visual], overnight #6 RAM census): the wet override drops destroyed pieces / renderers from its caches once a minute (was: held until 20k or the rain stopped). 1.2.133 ([visual], overnight #9 log census): the per-group [SnowBake] shader line only with [Batching] VerboseLogging (was ~1000 lines / 20 min), one 30 s summary instead. 1.2.132 ([visual], Fire 10-27 shot 535 "the undersides of roofs still render wet"): while the local player is in shelter (1 s in / 2 s out) and it rains, every live or baked piece over their head within 20 m draws with _Wet 0 (vanilla's wet gloss is gated by the sky-depth camera only, so a roof's underside reads as open sky); why-line "roof undersides dried N". 1.2.131 ([visual], Fire 10-26 shot 525 "stop the inside of pieces from looking wet"): while it rains, live pieces with vanilla's roof flag (WearNTear.m_haveRoof) get _Wet 0 in their MaterialPropertyBlock and baked groups draw their roofed range with _Wet 0 (vanilla Custom/Piece and FiresPiece both read the global _Wet); why-line "[EBM] wet override". 1.2.130 ([visual]/[seasons] 10-26, Fire's hut 403 roofed vs 67 open): no stand-in collider while the piece is still a real object (it sat inside its own copy; every roof test from the piece hit it); stand-ins carry an EbmStandIn marker (EbmStandIns.StandsInFor); [StandIn] why-lines. 1.2.129 ([visual], Fire 10-26 "logging in place to tell WHY"): shelter probe adds per-collider ray hits (live / stand-in, layer) + the rain-FX hider state each 10 s; every probe / hider bail-out logs its reason once. 1.2.128 ([visual], Fire 10-26 "rain indoors needs to live in ebm"): while the local player is in shelter, the current env's falling-weather particle systems stop emitting (ShelterRain, standalone; FTS 0.3.222 stands down on FiresEasyBakeMeshes.ShelterRain.Active); shelter probe adds a wet-underfoot dump. 1.2.127 ([visual], lead/Fire 10-26 wet inside baked homes): a re-bake keeps the zone's current stand-in colliders instead of destroying all and rebuilding them over frames (no roof gap); stand-ins copy the vanilla "leaky" tag; plus the read-only Debug "[EBM] shelter probe" every 10 s while raining (vanilla Cover rays + roof sphere-cast, live vs EBM stand-in hits, InShelter, Wet SE; EasyBake/ShelterProbe.cs). 1.2.125 ([visual]/[seasons], Fire 10-26 shots 459/460 straw roof white far, bare near): EBM instancing copies follow their source material's shader when FTS swaps it in place (InstanceDefinition.FollowSource, Info line per change); Debug [SnowBake] line per group every 10 s (shaders + mean _FiresSnowBiome). 1.2.124 ([visual], [seasons] SNOW_PERF_DIAG 10-26): baked-instance snow skips the roof test where coverage is 0 and caches each spot's roof answer 30 s (EasyBake/ExposureCache.cs), instead of one raycast per instance on every snow change. 1.2.123 ([visual], Fire 10-26 #1: "item drops float away like they have no gravity"): the remote-item ZSync skip pins the body (kinematic, velocity 0) while it holds a settled remote drop, the way vanilla ClientSync did every frame, restores it on hand-back, and also hands back when our copy drifts from the spot. 1.2.122 ([visual], lead 10-24 halo ring perf): EBM zones follow FAT 0.2.1050 ring OBJECT sectors (EasyBake/EbmZones.cs, FatApi.HaloZone by reflection; x,z off the ring): zone keys, loaded test, LOD + sort distance, cached-zone loop wrap at the seam, build-hold neighbourhood, create/destroy gates; keep-alive and the destroy loaded-zone index stand down on the ring. Terrain-keyed sector mirror unchanged. 1.2.121 ([visual], lead 10-24 halo ring): per-instance roof/shelter test point = the top of the bounds along the LOCAL up (Core GravityUp, soft; world up off a ring). 1.2.120 ([visual]/[seasons] 10-24): roof/shelter from FTS FiresPieceSnowDriver.SnowExposureAt (one implementation, reflection; vanilla Cover fallback) at the instance bounds TOP. 1.2.119 ([visual], Fire 10-24 snow under his roof): baked instances under a roof (vanilla Cover.IsUnderRoof) get snow 0 and draw in their own batches. 1.2.118 ([visual], lead 10-24): the instancing self-check uses vanilla Custom/Piece (loaded and drawn instanced), not Standard (not loaded in Valheim). 1.2.117 ([visual], [ghost]/[lead] 10-24): baked instances take Core dynamic snow (_FiresSnowBiome per instance, EasyBake\SnowFeed.cs, reflection-gated). 1.2.116 ([visual], hand-over 57 invisible pieces): one warning per shader that has no INSTANCING_ON variant when EBM would draw it instanced (InstanceDefinition.WarnIfNoInstancingVariant; read-only). 1.2.115 ([visual], Fire 10-24 invisible forge): PatchesStationInteractProbe.cs logs ebm_why for a crafting station when it is used (read-only probe; ZoneTracker.WhyFor).
